WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:05.960 --> 00:00:49.700
[Music]

00:00:51.500 --> 00:00:57.940
[Larry walks slowly out the front door of a doctor's office, appearing stunned.]

00:00:57.940 --> 00:01:17.960
[Music]

00:01:17.960 --> 00:01:24.540
[Siren]

00:01:26.940 --> 00:01:33.220
[Newspaper boy:] Extra! Extra! Read all about it! Hiya, Larry.

00:01:35.480 --> 00:02:02.680
[Larry continues walking slowly through town and into his office.]

00:02:02.680 --> 00:02:50.560
[Music]

00:02:54.780 --> 00:02:55.800
[Phil:] Hello, Larry.

00:02:57.566 --> 00:02:59.286
What are you doing?

00:03:01.600 --> 00:03:02.900
[Larry:] Hello, Phil.

00:03:03.160 --> 00:03:05.060
I'm just cleaning out some of this junk.

00:03:05.760 --> 00:03:07.293
[Phil:] Are you going someplace?

00:03:07.700 --> 00:03:10.500
[Larry:] Yeah, I, uh...

00:03:10.500 --> 00:03:12.233
I have to take a couple of days off.

00:03:12.233 --> 00:03:14.033
Sort of rest up a bit.

00:03:14.033 --> 00:03:16.033
[Phil:] Well, why? What's the trouble?

00:03:16.033 --> 00:03:19.513
[Larry:] I just left Dr. Clark, and he says I've got a little lung trouble.

00:03:19.680 --> 00:03:29.900
It's nothing serious you understand, it's just a ....
Well there it is, I've got TB!

00:03:29.900 --> 00:03:36.866
[Phil:] No! Well, it's a good thing you found out in 
time.

00:03:36.866 --> 00:03:38.266
What did Clark recommend?

00:03:38.266 --> 00:03:42.199
[Larry:] He, umm, wants me to go to bed.

00:03:42.200 --> 00:03:44.266
I'm going to stay home for a while and let Mom take 
care of me.

00:03:44.266 --> 00:03:46.799
[Phil:] Larry, what did Dr. Clark say?

00:03:46.800 --> 00:03:48.820
What do you mean?

00:03:51.700 --> 00:03:54.033
[Larry:] He wants me to go to a sanatorium.

00:03:54.600 --> 00:03:56.900
I'm gonna stay home.That's all there is to it.

00:03:56.900 --> 00:03:59.166
[Phil:] No, Larry, there's more to it than that.

00:03:59.440 --> 00:04:02.860
We didn't back the campaign to have everyone in Plainville x-rayed

00:04:02.866 --> 00:04:06.499
just so that our star reporter could make monkeys out of us.

00:04:08.120 --> 00:04:11.360
Look at that story!

00:04:11.720 --> 00:04:15.153
How would it look if the man who wrote that story 
didn't take his own advice?

00:04:15.466 --> 00:04:17.632
Ah, don't be a fool, Larry.

00:04:17.633 --> 00:04:20.866
If Dr. Clark thinks you ought to go to a sanatorium, you're going to go.

00:04:20.866 --> 00:04:22.646
Even if I have to knock you down and carry you there.

00:04:22.800 --> 00:04:24.333
[Larry:] You're not funny, Mr. Baxter.

00:04:24.340 --> 00:04:26.340
You're not funny at all.

00:04:26.800 --> 00:04:27.966
Now get out of my way!

00:04:27.966 --> 00:04:29.866
[Phil:] Larry, Larry. What's the matter with you, 
boy?

00:04:30.100 --> 00:04:32.366
You can't walk out like this.

00:04:32.900 --> 00:04:35.433
Besides, you and Helen are joining us for dinner.

00:04:35.433 --> 00:04:37.733
As a matter of fact, Helen is here already.

00:04:37.733 --> 00:04:38.873
[Larry:] She is?

00:04:43.080 --> 00:04:47.546
Now I've got to tell her.

00:04:47.900 --> 00:04:51.466
I'm sorry about blowing off like that, Phil.

00:04:53.480 --> 00:04:54.700
I'm all beat up.

00:04:54.700 --> 00:04:57.866
[Phil:] I know. It's tough.

00:04:57.866 --> 00:04:59.699
You go in and break the news to Helen.

00:04:59.700 --> 00:05:03.000
When Carol gets here, we'll come in and rescue 
you.

00:05:10.600 --> 00:05:12.533
[Helen:] Larry!

00:05:12.533 --> 00:05:16.173
Darling, I thought you'd never get here.

00:05:16.780 --> 00:05:19.013
But what's the matter, Larry?

00:05:20.460 --> 00:05:23.160
[Larry:] I, uh...I've got some bad news, Helen.

00:05:23.166 --> 00:05:25.432
You, you better sit down.

00:05:25.433 --> 00:05:27.399
[Helen:] Oh now, what happened?

00:05:27.400 --> 00:05:28.900
Did Phil fire you?

00:05:28.900 --> 00:05:32.180
I hope he did, and then we can get married right away.

00:05:32.600 --> 00:05:37.766
[Larry:] No, he didn't fire me exactly...

00:05:38.433 --> 00:05:41.199
It's just, I'm just, I'm afraid we can't get married.

00:05:41.200 --> 00:05:42.300
[Helen:] Can't get married?

00:05:42.300 --> 00:05:45.066
[Larry:] Oh, that is, not right away.

00:05:45.066 --> 00:05:46.232
[Helen:] Oh Larry, what is it?

00:05:46.233 --> 00:05:47.466
What's wrong?

00:05:47.466 --> 00:05:48.466
Have I done anything --

00:05:48.466 --> 00:05:50.099
[Larry:] Oh no, no, no, Helen.

00:05:50.100 --> 00:05:53.966
It isn't you, it's me.

00:05:53.966 --> 00:05:57.232
I've got tuberculosis.

00:05:57.233 --> 00:06:01.266
[Helen:] Oh my dear.

00:06:01.266 --> 00:06:04.466
Oh, for a moment I thought you didn't love me anymore.

00:06:07.700 --> 00:06:09.466
When do you go away?

00:06:09.466 --> 00:06:11.966
[Larry:]  Go away?

00:06:11.966 --> 00:06:14.332
I don't have to go anywhere.

00:06:14.333 --> 00:06:16.833
I'm just going home and go to bed.

00:06:16.833 --> 00:06:19.599
[Helen:] Don't you have to go to a sanatorium?

00:06:19.600 --> 00:06:23.100
I thought you had to go to one to cure tuberculosis.

00:06:23.100 --> 00:06:26.966
[Larry:] You sound as though you wanted me to go.

00:06:26.966 --> 00:06:28.832
I thought at least you...

00:06:28.833 --> 00:06:32.999
[Helen:] Oh Larry, all I want is for you to get well 
just as soon as you can.

00:06:33.000 --> 00:06:34.266
[Phil:] [knocks on the door] Hello in there.

00:06:34.266 --> 00:06:36.899
Can we come in?

00:06:36.900 --> 00:06:38.766
[Helen:] Oh hello, of course you can come in.

00:06:38.766 --> 00:06:39.699
Hello, Carol.

00:06:39.700 --> 00:06:40.520
[Carol:] Hello, dear.

00:06:42.666 --> 00:06:43.599
[Phil:] We'll work this thing out.

00:06:43.600 --> 00:06:45.133
Don't you worry, Helen.

00:06:45.133 --> 00:06:46.399
[Helen:] You can count on me, Phil.

00:06:46.400 --> 00:06:47.233
[Carol:] Hello, Larry.

00:06:47.233 --> 00:06:48.199
[Larry:] Hello, Carol.

00:06:48.200 --> 00:06:50.000
[Carol:] Phil told me the news, but don't worry.

00:06:50.000 --> 00:06:52.800
Everything's going to turn out all right, just as it did 
for us.

00:06:52.800 --> 00:06:54.766
[Larry:] For you?

00:06:54.766 --> 00:06:56.266
[Carol:] Why, didn't Phil tell you?

00:06:56.266 --> 00:06:58.132
[Phil:] No Carol, I haven't told them yet.

00:06:58.133 --> 00:06:59.633
Sit down.

00:07:02.280 --> 00:07:06.200
You see Larry, I had TB myself.

00:07:06.200 --> 00:07:10.600
Was cured at the same sanatorium Dr. Clark wants you to enter.

00:07:10.600 --> 00:07:12.166
It was pretty tough.

00:07:12.166 --> 00:07:16.066
A lot tougher than it should have been, and all  because I didn't think the doctors

00:07:16.066 --> 00:07:20.032
knew what they were talking about, wouldn't do what they told me to do.

00:07:20.033 --> 00:07:23.393
When I first discovered that I had TB, I was terribly worried.

00:07:25.100 --> 00:07:27.700
Carol and I were already married.

00:07:27.700 --> 00:07:32.066
It was tough, but my doctor said it was the sanatorium or else.

00:07:32.066 --> 00:07:33.632
So I went.

00:07:33.633 --> 00:07:35.966
Anyway, I began treatment.

00:07:35.966 --> 00:07:38.399
Everything went fine for a while.

00:07:38.400 --> 00:07:42.033
Then I began to worry again and got fidgety.

00:07:42.033 --> 00:07:43.733
Finally, I just up and left.

00:07:43.733 --> 00:07:45.799
Walked out without the doctor's okay.

00:07:45.800 --> 00:07:47.366
[Helen:] What happened then?

00:07:47.366 --> 00:07:50.399
[Carol:] What usually happens. He had a relapse.

00:07:50.400 --> 00:07:52.880
They carried him back to the sanatorium.

00:07:53.460 --> 00:07:58.093
[Phil:] And it took that experience to set me wise to myself.

00:07:58.600 --> 00:08:00.900
From then on, everything was fine.

00:08:00.900 --> 00:08:04.466
Oh, it was slow, but there was progress.

00:08:04.466 --> 00:08:07.299
Not just as far as my health was concerned.

00:08:07.300 --> 00:08:09.966
There was progress up here, too.

00:08:09.966 --> 00:08:12.046
I had time to think and write.

00:08:12.940 --> 00:08:18.200
It's because of those stories I wrote in bed that I have this office here today.

00:08:18.200 --> 00:08:20.560
I really believe that the three years that I spent in 
the sanatorium ....

00:08:20.560 --> 00:08:22.226
[Larry:] Three years!

00:08:23.700 --> 00:08:27.100
Three years flat on my back in a sanatorium!

00:08:27.100 --> 00:08:31.700
No, not me. I want to get married.

00:08:31.700 --> 00:08:34.400
You can't expect a girl to wait three years for a 
man who ...

00:08:34.400 --> 00:08:39.600
[Helen:] Larry, I'll wait for you thirty years if it takes 
that long.

00:08:39.600 --> 00:08:42.033
Oh you silly darling, I love you.

00:08:42.700 --> 00:08:47.933
I, I wish you could go to the sanatorium today 
so you could start getting better right away.

00:08:47.933 --> 00:08:50.333
[Carol:] And anyway Larry, you didn't get the point.

00:08:50.333 --> 00:08:53.233
Phil needed three years because he had a 
relapse.

00:08:53.233 --> 00:08:56.033
If he hadn't left without the doctor's permission, it wouldn't have happened.

00:08:56.033 --> 00:08:58.933
[Larry:] That's fine.

00:08:58.933 --> 00:09:01.433
That's just dandy.

00:09:02.900 --> 00:09:05.933
It's like you can't wait to get me into that hospital.

00:09:05.933 --> 00:09:09.033
Well, it's no good. I can't afford it, I've got a mother 
to support.

00:09:09.033 --> 00:09:11.299
She couldn't get along without me, she's just ....

00:09:11.300 --> 00:09:16.020
[Phil:] Larry, could she get along without you 
permanently?

00:09:23.700 --> 00:09:26.233
[Larry:] Okay, you win.

00:09:26.233 --> 00:09:30.913
[Phil:] No fella, you win.

00:09:36.200 --> 00:09:38.200
Well, today's the day.

00:09:38.200 --> 00:09:40.233
You'll be at the sanatorium in an hour.

00:09:40.233 --> 00:09:41.699
How do you feel?

00:09:41.700 --> 00:09:43.200
[Larry:] Okay, I guess.

00:09:43.200 --> 00:09:44.433
A little scared.

00:09:44.433 --> 00:09:46.599
[Phil:] It's always the first plunge that's bad.

00:09:46.600 --> 00:09:49.480
This time tomorrow, you'll be an old hand.

00:09:51.380 --> 00:09:54.233
They're a great bunch out there, especially Dr. Martin.

00:09:54.233 --> 00:09:55.599
You'll like him.

00:09:55.600 --> 00:09:57.380
Let's get going.

00:09:59.360 --> 00:10:12.120
[Car door shuts and engine starts.]

00:10:31.733 --> 00:10:38.073
[Larry:] It's a nice looking place, Phil, but ....

00:10:42.360 --> 00:10:44.933
[Phil:] Wait 'til you see the view from the rooms.

00:10:44.933 --> 00:10:46.833
The registration room is right down the corridor.

00:10:46.833 --> 00:10:48.833
[Larry:] It's so quiet in here. Where is everybody?

00:10:48.833 --> 00:10:50.133
[Phil:] Well, this is the rest period.

00:10:50.133 --> 00:10:51.313
Ahhh, here we are.

00:10:56.420 --> 00:11:00.500
[Nurse Butler:] Why, Mr. Baxter, we haven't seen  you in a long time.

00:11:00.500 --> 00:11:03.233
[Phil:] Nurse Butler, it's nice to see you.

00:11:03.233 --> 00:11:06.333
Larry, I want you to meet the gal who saved my life 
a dozen times.

00:11:06.333 --> 00:11:08.633
All she has to do is smile, and you feel better.

00:11:08.633 --> 00:11:09.633
This is Larry Scott.

00:11:09.633 --> 00:11:10.566
[Nurse Butler:] How do you do, Mr. Scott.

00:11:10.566 --> 00:11:11.632
[Larry:] Hello.

00:11:11.633 --> 00:11:13.566
[Phil:] He's my best reporter, I want you to take 
good care of him.

00:11:13.566 --> 00:11:15.432
[Nurse Butler:] We've been expecting you, Mr. 
Scott.

00:11:15.433 --> 00:11:18.166
Your records came from Dr. Clark this morning.

00:11:18.166 --> 00:11:23.526
Will you check through this form and if all the 
information is correct, will you please sign it?

00:11:28.000 --> 00:11:31.833
[Phil:] I'm a little worried about our friend.

00:11:31.833 --> 00:11:34.666
His mental outlook ....

00:11:34.666 --> 00:11:36.766
[Nurse Butler:] We were a little worried about you, 
Mr. Baxter.

00:11:36.766 --> 00:11:39.399
Remember? Now look at you.

00:11:39.400 --> 00:11:41.033
[Phil:] You're right.

00:11:41.033 --> 00:11:43.299
He's in good hands.

00:11:43.300 --> 00:11:45.100
I think I'll drop in and see Dr. Martin.

00:11:45.100 --> 00:11:45.900
[Nurse Butler:] Goodbye, Mr. Baxter.

00:11:45.900 --> 00:11:47.466
[Phil:] I'll come up when you're settled, Larry.

00:11:47.466 --> 00:11:49.999
[Larry:] See you later, Phil.

00:11:50.000 --> 00:11:53.660
[Nurse Butler:] Now if you will come with me, we'll 
get you settled in your room.

00:11:59.140 --> 00:12:01.206
[Gus:] Come in.

00:12:02.266 --> 00:12:03.299
Hi, Nurse Butler.

00:12:03.300 --> 00:12:04.233
How's tricks?

00:12:04.233 --> 00:12:05.566
[Nurse Butler:] Hello, Gus.

00:12:05.566 --> 00:12:07.632
This is Larry Scott, a new patient.

00:12:07.633 --> 00:12:08.799
Gus Grazinski.

00:12:08.800 --> 00:12:09.600
[Gus:] Hiya, Larry.

00:12:09.600 --> 00:12:10.666
[Larry:] Hello.

00:12:10.666 --> 00:12:13.032
[Nurse Butler:] You can put your street clothes on 
that chair there, Mr. Scott,

00:12:13.033 --> 00:12:15.766
and your small things in the night table here.

00:12:15.766 --> 00:12:19.446
I'll be back later to see how you're getting on.

00:12:30.840 --> 00:12:32.760
[Larry:] Here goes nothing.

00:12:35.600 --> 00:12:37.080
[Phil:] All settled, Larry?

00:12:38.600 --> 00:12:40.033
Good.

00:12:40.160 --> 00:12:42.860
Dr. Martin will be along directly.

00:12:43.166 --> 00:12:45.499
How do you feel?

00:12:45.500 --> 00:12:47.966
[Larry:] Okay, I guess.

00:12:47.966 --> 00:12:50.599
[Phil:] Anything I can do for you?

00:12:50.600 --> 00:12:52.266
[Larry:] No, thanks.

00:12:53.960 --> 00:12:55.300
[Phil:] Are you sure?

00:12:55.440 --> 00:12:56.800
[Larry:] Yeah, I'm sure.

00:12:58.600 --> 00:13:00.660
[Phil:] Well, all right.

00:13:01.080 --> 00:13:04.880
I, I guess I better be going.

00:13:05.800 --> 00:13:09.333
Take it easy, Larry. Do what they tell you to,

00:13:09.333 --> 00:13:11.866
and relax, Larry.

00:13:11.866 --> 00:13:14.199
Relax.

00:13:14.200 --> 00:13:16.720
I'll see you in a couple of weeks.

00:13:17.320 --> 00:13:18.600
[Larry:] Bye, Phil.

00:13:25.460 --> 00:13:27.326
[Gus:] So your name is Larry Scott.

00:13:27.866 --> 00:13:31.346
I knew some Scotts down in Thorndike.
No kin of yours, I suppose?

00:13:33.233 --> 00:13:34.799
[Larry:] Nope.

00:13:34.800 --> 00:13:36.800
[Gus:] Ever been to Thorndike?

00:13:36.800 --> 00:13:38.366
[Larry shakes his head.]

00:13:38.366 --> 00:13:39.666
[Gus:] It's a nice town.

00:13:39.666 --> 00:13:41.806
I used to be a telephone linemen there.

00:13:44.780 --> 00:13:46.900
Ever been to a sanatorium before?

00:13:48.620 --> 00:13:50.060
[Larry:] No.

00:13:51.160 --> 00:13:53.793
[Gus:] Some guys here been back two and three 
times.

00:13:54.000 --> 00:13:55.800
They never learn.

00:13:55.800 --> 00:13:57.600
Start living high as soon as they get out.

00:13:57.600 --> 00:14:02.200
First thing you know, [fingers snap] bang, relapse 
and back they come.

00:14:02.200 --> 00:14:04.566
Stupid, ain't it?

00:14:04.566 --> 00:14:06.266
[Larry:] Yeah.

00:14:06.266 --> 00:14:08.832
[Gus:] You're a talkative son of a gun, aren't ya?

00:14:08.833 --> 00:14:11.033
You'll get over that.

00:14:11.033 --> 00:14:13.693
You'll feel better once you learn how to relax.

00:14:20.100 --> 00:14:21.433
[Nurse Butler] Good morning.

00:14:21.433 --> 00:14:24.313
It's a beautiful day.

00:14:28.633 --> 00:14:32.433
Just try to relax and take a nap before lunch.

00:14:35.940 --> 00:14:38.620
[Dr. Martin:] Is anything worrying you, Scott?

00:14:39.866 --> 00:14:41.799
[Nurse 1:] Good afternoon, Larry.

00:14:41.800 --> 00:14:44.040
Here's that book you wanted.

00:14:50.800 --> 00:14:51.600
[Nurse 2:] Good night.

00:14:51.600 --> 00:14:53.580
Time for sleep.

00:15:00.766 --> 00:15:03.032
[Larry:] Have to rest.

00:15:03.033 --> 00:15:04.113
Learn how to rest.

00:15:08.280 --> 00:15:12.213
[Phil's voice:] And relax, Larry. Relax.

00:15:12.933 --> 00:15:14.266
[Nurses's voice:] Good evening.

00:15:14.266 --> 00:15:16.432
Time for supper.

00:15:16.433 --> 00:15:20.066
[Phil's voice:] And relax, Larry. Relax.

00:15:20.066 --> 00:15:23.832
[Nurse's voice:] Good night. Time for sleep.

00:15:23.833 --> 00:15:26.566
[Phil's voice:] And relax, Larry. Relax.

00:15:26.566 --> 00:15:30.032
[Nurse's voice:] Good night. Time for sleep.

00:15:30.033 --> 00:15:32.133
[Phil's voice:] And relax, Larry. Relax.

00:15:32.133 --> 00:15:34.833
And relax, Larry. Relax.

00:15:34.833 --> 00:15:36.333
[Larry:] I've got to get out of here.

00:15:36.333 --> 00:15:37.299
I'm going crazy.

00:15:37.300 --> 00:15:38.333
I'm going crazy.

00:15:38.333 --> 00:15:39.033
[Gus:] Whoa.

00:15:39.033 --> 00:15:40.099
[Larry:] I gotta get out of here.

00:15:40.100 --> 00:15:42.100
[Gus:] Take it easy, Larry. Take it easy.

00:15:42.300 --> 00:15:43.900
[Nurse 3:] What's wrong, what's wrong?

00:15:44.000 --> 00:15:45.766
You'll wake everyone up by that shouting.

00:15:46.300 --> 00:15:49.400
You need to lie down.

00:15:52.366 --> 00:15:54.706
[Larry:] Sorry, disturbing....

00:15:55.400 --> 00:15:57.266
[Dr. Martin:] Well, Scott, what's bothering you?

00:15:57.266 --> 00:15:59.199
Thought we had everything straightened out.

00:15:59.200 --> 00:16:00.066
[Larry:] I don't know doctor.

00:16:00.066 --> 00:16:03.586
It's, it's just that I can't get any sleep.

00:16:04.360 --> 00:16:07.760
I haven't had a good night's sleep since I got here.

00:16:08.033 --> 00:16:09.333
Better go home.

00:16:10.100 --> 00:16:12.400
I told you I didn't think I could make a go of it.

00:16:12.666 --> 00:16:16.099
[Dr. Martin:] If it's your home you're worrying about, 
the social worker has told you

00:16:16.100 --> 00:16:19.033
that everything is going smoothly there.

00:16:20.220 --> 00:16:23.120
[Larry:] Everybody keeps saying relax, relax.

00:16:25.266 --> 00:16:27.166
I can't even sleep here.

00:16:28.900 --> 00:16:33.560
[Dr. Martin:] You know Larry, relaxation is really a state of mind.

00:16:33.566 --> 00:16:36.232
Your state of mind.

00:16:36.233 --> 00:16:38.673
Well, I'll see that you sleep tonight.

00:16:38.720 --> 00:16:40.986
A light sedative will do the trick.

00:16:41.240 --> 00:16:46.400
Tomorrow morning, if you still want to, we'll talk 
about your leaving.

00:16:46.400 --> 00:16:47.933
Good night, Larry.

00:16:47.933 --> 00:16:49.533
[Larry:] Good night.

00:17:07.866 --> 00:17:13.499
[Nurse 3:] Good night, Mr. Scott.

00:17:13.500 --> 00:17:17.880
[Larry is dreaming.]

00:17:18.620 --> 00:17:25.833
[Music plays as if at a carnival.]

00:17:25.833 --> 00:17:28.166
[Larry:] What are you doing, Gus?

00:17:28.166 --> 00:17:31.566
[Gus:] Shhhhhh, it's a party line.

00:17:32.400 --> 00:17:36.300
[Gus laughs]

00:17:37.166 --> 00:17:40.486
They're talking about youuuuuu.

00:17:46.433 --> 00:17:50.233
[Larry knocks on a door.]

00:17:50.233 --> 00:17:51.133
[Larry:] Congratulations!

00:17:51.133 --> 00:17:53.366
We're going to be married today.

00:17:53.366 --> 00:17:55.232
[Helen:] Oh no, not today.

00:17:55.233 --> 00:17:57.166
I said I'd wait thirty years.

00:17:57.166 --> 00:18:03.766
[Helen giggles.]

00:18:03.766 --> 00:18:11.746
[Paperboy:] Extra! Extra! Read all about it!
Larry Scott is broke. Larry Scott is broke.

00:18:19.566 --> 00:18:26.226
[Women on street:] Larry Scott is penniless,
Larry Scott is penniless.

00:18:27.833 --> 00:18:29.599
[Operator:] Mr. Larry Scott.

00:18:29.600 --> 00:18:32.233
I'm sorry, Mr. Scott isn't in.

00:18:32.233 --> 00:18:34.133
He's gone to a funeral.

00:18:34.133 --> 00:18:35.999
Whose funeral?

00:18:36.000 --> 00:18:40.200
Why, his own funeral, of course.

00:18:40.540 --> 00:18:51.320
[Staccato music]

00:18:54.100 --> 00:18:55.160
[Policeman:] What's the matter?

00:18:55.166 --> 00:18:56.366
You want to die young?

00:18:56.366 --> 00:18:57.299
You want to die young?

00:18:57.300 --> 00:18:59.266
You want to die young?

00:18:59.266 --> 00:19:02.032
[Paperboy:] Extra! Extra! Read all about it!

00:19:02.033 --> 00:19:07.733
[Women on the street:] Larry Scott is penniless.
Larry Scott is penniless.

00:19:07.733 --> 00:19:12.373
[Helen:] Wait thirty years.
Wait thirty years. [Laughter]

00:19:16.600 --> 00:19:18.566
[Larry:] A dream!

00:19:18.566 --> 00:19:22.766
All the fear and terror in that dream.

00:19:22.766 --> 00:19:25.866
I feel as if I've been in a fight.

00:19:25.866 --> 00:19:28.599
Been fighting all the wrong things.

00:19:28.600 --> 00:19:32.700
I've been fighting everything except tuberculosis.

00:19:32.700 --> 00:19:37.433
Fighting this bed, the doctors, myself.

00:19:37.433 --> 00:19:38.899
I have to stop that.

00:19:38.900 --> 00:19:41.433
Have to take a time out.

00:19:41.433 --> 00:19:43.233
Learn how to rest.

00:19:43.233 --> 00:19:44.999
Have to rest.

00:19:45.000 --> 00:19:46.266
Rest.

00:19:46.266 --> 00:19:47.886
Rest.

00:19:50.500 --> 00:19:52.600
[Dr. Martin:] Well Larry, how do you feel this 
morning?

00:19:52.600 --> 00:19:54.566
[Larry:] I feel fine.

00:19:54.566 --> 00:19:55.299
[Gus:] You should.

00:19:55.300 --> 00:19:58.166
They let you sleep through breakfast.

00:19:58.166 --> 00:19:59.166
[Larry:] I'm hungry, too.

00:19:59.166 --> 00:20:00.266
I could eat some breakfast.

00:20:00.266 --> 00:20:02.599
[Nurse 3:] I'll see if I can find something.

00:20:02.600 --> 00:20:06.100
There's some tomato juice on your table.

00:20:06.100 --> 00:20:10.033
[Dr. Martin:] Well, your program for the time being 
is complete bed rest.

00:20:10.033 --> 00:20:13.433
Remember Larry, you're here to rest.

00:20:13.433 --> 00:20:17.566
That means conserving your energy in every way 
you can.

00:20:17.566 --> 00:20:18.626
[Larry:] I'll try.

00:20:22.966 --> 00:20:26.866
[Dr. Martin:] Turn over or move around only 
enough to keep from getting cramped.

00:20:26.866 --> 00:20:29.146
You can sit up to eat or to read occasionally.

00:20:34.900 --> 00:20:37.800
[Larry:] Mmmm, good.

00:20:37.800 --> 00:20:39.966
[Dr. Martin:] Still want to talk about going home?

00:20:39.966 --> 00:20:41.432
[Larry:] No, doctor.

00:20:41.433 --> 00:20:45.533
I'm beginning to feel a little better about the whole 
thing now.

00:20:48.940 --> 00:20:50.940
[Knock on door]

00:20:51.660 --> 00:20:54.040
Come in.

00:20:55.440 --> 00:20:57.360
[Phil:] Hello, Larry. How are you?

00:20:57.366 --> 00:20:59.099
[Larry:] Hello, Phil.
Glad you could make it.

00:20:59.100 --> 00:21:00.266
[Phil:] You're looking fine.

00:21:00.266 --> 00:21:00.946
[Larry:] Feel fine.

00:21:02.220 --> 00:21:07.053
Hey Phil, I want you to meet Gus Grissom, best telephone linesman in Thorndike.

00:21:07.733 --> 00:21:09.866
This is my boss, Phil Baxter.

00:21:09.866 --> 00:21:11.299
[Gus:] Ex-linesman.

00:21:11.300 --> 00:21:12.020
Hi. How are you, Mr. Baxter?

00:21:12.120 --> 00:21:13.140
[Phil:] Hello.

00:21:17.900 --> 00:21:19.700
What's the matter with him?

00:21:19.700 --> 00:21:21.033
[Larry:] Mathematics.

00:21:21.033 --> 00:21:22.333
[Phil:] Ohhhh

00:21:22.333 --> 00:21:25.366
[Larry:] So tell me Phil, how are Carol and Patrick?

00:21:25.366 --> 00:21:26.832
And have you seen Helen lately?

00:21:26.833 --> 00:21:28.033
And how's mother?

00:21:28.033 --> 00:21:29.333
The social worker tells me she......

00:21:29.333 --> 00:21:32.433
[Phil:] Oh wait a minute, one thing at a time.
Your mother is fine.

00:21:32.433 --> 00:21:33.493
Helen was over at the house for dinner last night 
and...

00:21:33.500 --> 00:21:34.640
[Knock at the door]

00:21:35.860 --> 00:21:37.960
[Nurse Jones:] Here you are, boys, I brought....

00:21:38.466 --> 00:21:40.599
Sorry, I didn't know you had a visitor.

00:21:40.600 --> 00:21:42.033
[Larry:] That's all right, Nurse Jones.

00:21:42.033 --> 00:21:43.366
This is Mr. Baxter.

00:21:43.366 --> 00:21:45.732
Those animals I've been making are for his little 
girl.

00:21:45.733 --> 00:21:48.033
Of course, they'll be sterilized before Patsy gets 
them.

00:21:48.033 --> 00:21:52.199
[Nurse Jones:] Hello, Mr. Baxter. I've been hearing about your little girl for some time now.

00:21:52.200 --> 00:21:53.866
[Larry:] You think she'll like them, Phil?

00:21:53.866 --> 00:21:56.166
Show him that camel, Nurse Jones.

00:21:56.166 --> 00:21:58.166
I think that's the best one.

00:21:58.166 --> 00:22:01.566
I remember Patsy always liked the camels best at the zoo.

00:22:03.466 --> 00:22:07.332
[Dr. Martin:] Well Larry, we can soon let you get out of bed a little each day now.

00:22:07.333 --> 00:22:11.533
Your x-rays have been showing steady 
improvement, and we can soon...

00:22:11.533 --> 00:22:14.266
[Nurse 6:] You're making real progress.

00:22:14.266 --> 00:22:16.746
[Larry:] I'll get there.

00:22:28.860 --> 00:22:32.560
[Man at desk:] You're up to two hours a day of out-
of-bed activity, Mr. Scott.

00:22:33.066 --> 00:22:39.266
Oh, incidentally, the latest issue of the sanatorium 
newspaper was really tops.

00:22:39.266 --> 00:22:44.532
But, in addition to editing Sidelights, what do you think of a plan to start a class

00:22:44.533 --> 00:22:47.773
in short-story writing, with you as instructor?

00:22:49.900 --> 00:22:51.333
[Larry:] I like that.

00:22:51.360 --> 00:22:53.240
I'd be very glad to do it.

00:23:00.280 --> 00:23:01.746
[Nurse Butler:] Goodbye, Mr. Scott.

00:23:02.366 --> 00:23:03.332
Take care of yourself.

00:23:03.333 --> 00:23:06.213
[Larry:] Goodbye, and thank you for everything.

00:23:13.566 --> 00:23:19.366
[Helen:] Larry! Oh, Larry.

00:23:19.366 --> 00:23:20.266
[Larry:] Hello, darling.

00:23:20.266 --> 00:23:24.066
[Helen:] Oh, I've waited so long for this day.

00:23:24.066 --> 00:23:25.466
You about ready?

00:23:25.466 --> 00:23:27.832
[Larry:] I have to see Dr. Martin first.

00:23:27.833 --> 00:23:31.166
Come on, I want you to meet him.

00:23:31.166 --> 00:23:36.966
I'm deeply grateful for all you've done for me, and 
well, I hope I can do something for you someday.

00:23:36.966 --> 00:23:38.632
[Dr. Martin:] Take care of yourself, Larry.

00:23:38.633 --> 00:23:42.633
Remember that you have a new kind of life to live, 
and everything will be all right.

00:23:42.633 --> 00:23:43.466
See Dr. Clarke.

00:23:43.466 --> 00:23:44.999
He's expecting you.

00:23:45.000 --> 00:23:47.000
He'll work out a complete set of instructions.

00:23:47.000 --> 00:23:48.866
Be sure to follow them.

00:23:48.866 --> 00:23:52.332
[Larry:] I'll remember, and I'll do just that.

00:23:52.333 --> 00:23:53.666
[Dr. Martin:] Goodbye Larry.

00:23:53.666 --> 00:23:56.399
[Larry:] Thanks again for everything.

00:23:56.400 --> 00:23:57.400
[Dr. Martin:] Goodbye, Ms. Eisler.

00:23:57.400 --> 00:23:59.300
[Helen:] Goodbye, Dr. Martin.

00:23:59.300 --> 00:24:01.233
I like that Dr. Martin, Larry.

00:24:01.233 --> 00:24:04.066
What did he mean about your having to live a new 
kind of life?

00:24:04.066 --> 00:24:07.999
[Larry:] Well, a TB patient has to watch himself pretty carefully.

00:24:08.000 --> 00:24:13.240
Get enough rest, good food, and dress warmly.

00:24:13.920 --> 00:24:15.880
And, of course, see his doctor regularly.

00:24:16.340 --> 00:24:21.860
That's what everyone should do, but a TBer has to do it.

00:24:21.860 --> 00:24:40.733
[Music]

00:24:40.733 --> 00:24:47.253
[Helen writes in her diary.]

00:24:47.260 --> 00:25:22.333
[Music]

00:25:22.333 --> 00:25:28.666
[Larry:] "Hi, Larry. Greetings from the new 
supervisor of the Thorndike Telephone Company.

00:25:28.666 --> 00:25:31.999
I made it! Gus."

00:25:32.000 --> 00:25:35.100
Well, good ole Gus Grazinski.

00:25:35.100 --> 00:25:37.040
I knew it.

00:25:40.733 --> 00:25:47.993
[Typewriter keys clack, then phone rings.]

00:25:48.240 --> 00:25:49.173
Hello.

00:25:49.900 --> 00:25:54.533
[Dr. Martin:] Larry, I wonder if you could come out 
here today and be my prize exhibit.

00:25:54.533 --> 00:25:56.833
We have a new patient, a young engineer.

00:25:56.833 --> 00:26:01.566
He's a very sick man, and he's tougher to handle than you were.

00:26:01.566 --> 00:26:03.399
I thought if he heard your story...

00:26:03.400 --> 00:26:07.660
[Larry:] Hold everything doctor, I'm on my way.

00:26:10.700 --> 00:26:14.940
[Dr. Martin:] With people like Larry on the team, we 
can beat TB.

00:26:15.500 --> 00:26:26.260
[Music]

